.TH fmt_escapecharcx 3
.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharcx \- escape a character using C-style hexadecimal sequences
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
size_t \fBfmt_escapecharcx\fR(char *\fIdest\fR, int \fIchr\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfmt_escapecharcx\fR encodes the character \fIchr\fR into a C-style escaped representation using hexadecimal for non-printable characters.
.PP
If \fIchr\fR corresponds to a common escape sequence (e.g., '\n', '\t', '\e'), it is encoded as a 2-byte sequence (a backslash followed by the escape character). Otherwise, it is encoded as a 4-byte sequence: a backslash followed by 'x' and two hexadecimal digits.
.PP
If \fIdest\fR is not NULL, the encoded character is written to \fIdest\fR.
.PP
The function returns the number of bytes required (or written). It returns 0 if \fIchr\fR > 0xff.
.SH SEE ALSO
fmt_escapecharc(3)